  <!-- CoP quick-use slots: four cells that remember an ITEM SECTION (ACTOR_DEFS::g_quick_use_slots)
       and are fired by the quick_use_1..4 keys. Drag an eatable here from the bag; double-click a
       slot to clear it. A row under the belt, cells the same size as the belt's. Remove this node
       and the feature disappears cleanly -- the menu creates the widget only if it is present. -->
  <!-- Placed on the four frames drawn in ui_ingame2_common.dds. Measured as CENTRE + size:
       385,52.5 52x47 | 467,52.5 | 547,52.5 | 623,52.5 -> top-left 359/441/521/597 at y=29, and X
       and WIDTH scaled by 604/725 like everything else on that texture. The frames are not evenly
       spaced (gaps 82/80/76 dds px), so a single grid cannot hit all four: the pitch below is
       anchored on the first and the last, leaving the middle two ~0.3 px short.
       The cells are then shrunk 1.5x about their own centres (43x47 -> 29x31), so the icons sit
       smaller inside the frames while the pitch of 66 keeps every centre where it was. -->
  <!-- ...and NARROWED to 25 wide: the icon is drawn stretched into the cell, so a cell whose
       width:height is wider than the rest of the menu (the bag cells are 26x32) draws every
       item icon stretched sideways. 25/31 matches that proportion. The pitch (cell + spacing)
       stays 66 so the cells keep hitting the frames, and x moves by half the 4 units lost so
       each cell stays centred in its frame. orig: cell_width=29 cell_sp_x=37 x=306.08.
       The label_*_dx below are each +2 against the original for the same reason: the key captions
       are right-aligned and their width is cellSize.x, so the narrower cell pulled them 4 left and
       the x shift gave 2 back. orig: 7 / 3 / 5 / 6 / 3 -->
  <dragdrop_quick_slots x="308.08" y="37" width="227" height="31"
          cell_width="25" cell_height="31" rows_num="1" cols_num="4"
          cell_sp_x="41" cell_sp_y="0" custom_placement="1" a="0"
          label_dx="9" label_dy="9"
          label0_dx="5"  label0_dy="9"
          label1_dx="7"  label1_dy="9"
          label2_dx="8"  label2_dy="9"
          label3_dx="5"  label3_dy="9"/>

